## 13. Governing Principle

If an organisation ingests human experience signals, it should structurally guarantee:
1. Comprehension of the affected surface
2. Actionable mission generation
3. Measurable state transition
4. Persistent memory of consequence

Decipher encodes these obligations as computational requirements.

---

## Closing Position
Decipher is a structured governance substrate for experience-driver state and closed-loop intervention.

It does not replace existing analytics systems. It formalises what those systems cannot persist.

It does not create autonomy. It provides the structural preconditions under which autonomy can be bounded and measurable.

Its value depends on disciplined implementation and institutional adoption. It is an architectural model, 
not a claim of inevitability.
